Why Is Demand Increasing
Rapid Disease Response: RNA platforms can be redesigned by changing antigen sequences, supporting faster responses to rapidly evolving animal pathogens.
Poultry Disease Control: Recurring avian influenza outbreaks and large-scale poultry vaccination requirements are creating significant opportunities for rapidly adaptable vaccine technologies.
RNA Platform Commercialization: Existing RNA-particle veterinary products and growing self-amplifying RNA programs are strengthening commercial validation of RNA-based animal vaccines.

Veterinary mRNA Vaccines Watch: Self-Amplifying RNA and Rapid-Response Platforms
Veterinary RNA vaccine development is expanding beyond conventional mRNA-LNP approaches to include self-amplifying RNA and RNA-particle technologies. These platforms can offer programmable antigen expression and potential manufacturing advantages, while non-invasive delivery methods are being explored to reduce labor and simplify mass vaccination in poultry and livestock.

